{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:MassTheory.MassEndomorphismTower","@type":"LeanModule","name":"MassTheory.MassEndomorphismTower","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.Field.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Order.BigOperators.Group.Finset","lean:module:Mathlib.Data.Fintype.Card","lean:module:Mathlib.Tactic.Linarith"],"declarations":9,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.mass_endomorphism_positive","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.mass_endomorphism_positive","kind":"theorem","line":134,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L134-L158","doc":"**The mass endomorphism is strictly positive when its descended term\nis.**  Under `MassPositivityHyp`, if the descended trace term\n`‖∏ V i‖_F > 0` then the pre-Arch mass `Pre.massPoly > 0`.  This is\nthe strict form of `mass_endomorphism_nonneg`: the two `Li₂^q`\ncontributions are still `≤ 0`, so a strictly positive descended term\ndominates. ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:mass-endomorphism-tower","label":"prop:mass-endomorphism-tower","md":"quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.mass_endomorphism_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.mass_endomorphism_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":105,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L105-L132","doc":"**The mass endomorphism is non-negative.**  Under `MassPositivityHyp`\n(a genuine norm + the bounded-Rogers dilog sign), the pre-Arch mass\n`Pre.massPoly` is `≥ 0` for every braid data `(q, n, V)`.\n\nProof: the descended term `‖∏ V i‖_F ≥ 0`; both `Li₂^q` sums are\n`≤ 0` (each summand `Li₂^q(−‖·‖_F) ≤ 0` since `‖·‖_F ≥ 0`, then\n`Finset.sum_nonpos`); the pair weight `z² ≥ 0` (`sq_nonneg`), so\n`z²·(sum ≤ 0) ≤ 0`; hence `A − B − z²·D ≥ 0` with `A ≥ 0`, `B ≤ 0`,\n`z²·D ≤ 0`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.li2q_nonpos_on_neg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.li2q_nonpos_on_neg","kind":"theorem","line":103,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L103-L103","doc":"Bounded-Rogers sign: `Li₂^q(−x) ≤ 0` on non-negative arguments. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.norm_nonneg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.norm_nonneg","kind":"theorem","line":101,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L101-L101","doc":"The Frobenius norm is genuinely a norm: non-negative everywhere. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp.mk","kind":"ctor","line":99,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L99-L99","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.MassPositivityHyp","kind":"structure","line":93,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L93-L103","doc":"The hypotheses under which the mass endomorphism is non-negative:\na genuine (non-negative) Frobenius norm, and the bounded-Rogers sign\nof the symmetric `q`-dilogarithm.  The second field is exactly why\nthe bounded `Li₂^q` replaced the Faddeev `Φ_q`: on the physical\n(non-negative-norm) arguments the `Φ_q` face blows up and changes\nsign, whereas `Li₂^q(−x) ≤ 0` for `0 ≤ x`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.massPoly","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.massPoly","kind":"def","line":71,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L71-L85","doc":"The pre-Arch mass formula, valued in the ground field `R`.\n\nEach generator's traced volume `V i ∈ R` is supplied as data; the\nFrobenius norm `‖·‖_F : R → R` and the symmetric `q`-dilogarithm\n`Li₂^q : R → R` are also passed in (abstract; no Archimedean `|·|`,\nno series).  Signs and the `z²` pair weight follow the `.md` boxed\nformula (convention D):\n\n  𝔪 = ‖∏ V i‖_F − Σᵢ Li₂^q(−‖V i‖_F)\n        − z² · Σ_{adj} Li₂^q(−‖V i · V j‖_F),   z = q³/(q²+1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.adjPairNorm","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.adjPairNorm","kind":"def","line":64,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L64-L69","doc":"Frobenius norm of an adjacent generator pair's product.  Hides the\n`Fin` casts (`i.val < n` and `i.val + 1 < n`, from `i : Fin (n-1)`)\nso downstream proofs stay clean. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.markovZD","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.MassEndomorphism.Pre.markovZD","kind":"def","line":59,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/mass-theory/mass-endomorphism-tower.lean#L59-L62","doc":"Markov parameter `z = q³/(q²+1)` (**convention D**, owner ruling\n2026-08-15), valued in the ground field `R`.  Supersedes the excised\nconvention-C form `√q/(q+1)`. ","signatureChunk":0}]}